<%--
Form_Errors

The one place a form's failure feedback renders: the always-visible top alert on a
failed submit, and non-validation errors. Place it WHERE THE LAYOUT WANTS IT - inside
the first section, above a two-column grid, under a heading - and the renderer targets
it; the form's structural containers then give it their own spacing, which is the whole
reason placement belongs to the form author and not to the engine.

Every <Rsx_Form> contains exactly one. A form without one throws the moment failure
feedback is needed - the engine never invents a position for the alert, because an
engine-chosen position sits outside every section's spacing and the layout has no say.

    <Rsx_Form $controller="..." $method="...">
        <div class="view-section">
            <Form_Errors />
            <Form_Field $label="Title" $required=true>
                <Text_Input $name="title" $max_length=255 />
            </Form_Field>
        </div>
    </Rsx_Form>
--%>
<Define:Form_Errors tag="div" class="Rsx_Form__error"></Define:Form_Errors>
